Rule 1 (x1 must be a floating-point tensor)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≥ 6 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 2 (x2 must be a floating-point tensor)
{v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) ≥ 6 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 3 (tensors x1 and x2 must have matching dtypes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 4 (if neither input is a scalar, they must have the same number of dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 5 (if neither input is a scalar, they must be broadcast-compatible)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1
